<!-- @after KMP — The Decisive Factor :: visual -->
### Choose the boundary before the library

<figure class="viz"><div class="viz-grid" style="--cols:2"><div class="node"><strong>Shared API</strong><small>Domain-facing operations and models used by the product.</small></div><div class="node"><strong>Per-platform configuration</strong><small>Engine, TLS/proxy behaviour and platform lifecycle.</small></div><div class="node"><strong>Compatibility suite</strong><small>Missing/null fields, error contracts, cancellation and streaming.</small></div><div class="node"><strong>Rollout evidence</strong><small>A representative endpoint, telemetry and rollback path.</small></div></div><figcaption>Sharing request code does not remove the need to verify each supported engine and platform.</figcaption></figure>

<!-- @before When Each Wins (Concrete Scenarios) :: review -->
The strict-size and free-migration rows in the next table (KT3–KT4) are under technical review. A correction is pending the owner's approval.

<!-- @after Migration Patterns :: visual -->
### Migrate one contract, then widen

<figure class="viz decision-map"><p class="diagram-context">One repository, two implementations during a staged migration</p><ol class="decision-grid"><li class="decision-card"><span class="decision-number" aria-hidden="true">1</span><h4>Pin behaviour</h4><p>Choose one representative operation and write down its data, auth, error and cancellation contract.</p></li><li class="decision-card"><span class="decision-number" aria-hidden="true">2</span><h4>Add an adapter</h4><p>Implement that contract using the candidate stack behind the existing application boundary.</p></li><li class="decision-card"><span class="decision-number" aria-hidden="true">3</span><h4>Exercise parity</h4><p>Run equivalent fixtures on the engines and targets the product actually ships.</p></li><li class="decision-card"><span class="decision-number" aria-hidden="true">4</span><h4>Roll out selectively</h4><p>Select one implementation per call path. Observe failures and performance; keep rollback available.</p></li><li class="decision-card"><span class="decision-number" aria-hidden="true">5</span><h4>Retire deliberately</h4><p>Remove old dependencies only after their final owned call path and configuration are retired.</p></li></ol><figcaption>Illustrative decision example. This sequence is an application migration plan; its outcome depends on measured parity, not on endpoint count alone.</figcaption></figure>

